STEP read with sub-shape names: the name pass walks past a face bound, a
loop, a shell or an edge list the file reader left null instead of
dereferencing it (mitcad#2028).

Expected: a STEP file whose FACE_BOUND refers to an entity that is not in
the file reads as the shape transfer reads it, with the names and colours
of everything else. Actual (observed, a crash report of a Windows build
and the reproducer below on Linux): with
DESTEP_Parameters::ReadSubshapeNames on, STEPCAFControl_Reader::Transfer
crashes with an access violation in Standard_Transient::IsInstance, called
from ExpandShell <- ExpandManifoldSolidBrep <- ExpandSubShapes.

The file reader leaves a reference it cannot resolve null (StepData_
StepReaderData::ReadEntity reports "Unresolved reference" or "Entity has
illegal type" in the entity's check and sets nothing). The shape transfer
treats those fields as optional: StepToTopoDS_TranslateFace skips a null
face bound and a null loop, so the solid is made of the rest. The name
pass after it (ExpandSubShapes) walks the same entities and already skips
a null face, bound array, oriented edge and edge, but it dereferenced a
null face bound (aWires->Value(w)->Bound()), a null loop
(aWire->IsInstance), a null edge list (anEdgeLoop->EdgeList()), a null
outer shell or face array (aMSB->Outer(), Shell->CfsFaces()) and a null
boundary array of a shell based surface model (aSBSM->SbsmBoundary()),
whose null shell it passed on to ExpandShell.

- ExpandManifoldSolidBrep and ExpandSBSM return on an item of another
  type and on a null boundary array.
- ExpandShell returns on a null shell or face array and goes on to the
  next bound on a null face bound or loop, and to the next loop on a null
  edge list.
What is null has no sub-shape in the transferred shape to put a name on;
the names of everything else are set as before.

Test: geometry.port.1820 (geometry/tests/port/p1820-step-sub-shape-names-
unresolved-bound.cpp): a box as a MANIFOLD_SOLID_BREP of a named product,
one face with a second FACE_BOUND whose bound is an entity not in the
file, read through STEPCAFControl_Reader with sub-shape names: stock OCCT
crashes; with the patch it is one valid solid of 1000 mm3 with six faces
under the product's name. geometry.io reads the same text with
read_step_structured.

Upstream: changes only files with unresolved references, which crashed
before; every other file is read as before. OCCT master has the same
ExpandShell (read 18.11.2026).
